                </common:classification>
            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">Data for material and energy requirements for construction and decommissioning are from an old US study, which does not differentiate between dry and wet process. The material inventory may not correspond to currently Chinese operating facilities, which is taken into account in the uncertainties. The land use is based on actual data for the US Sequoyah facility. The lifetime is assumed to be 40 years with a throughput of 5000 t/a. Although Sequoyah was operating only for 22 years, 40 years can be assumed as an average for currently operating plants. Transport requirements recalculated either using ecoinvent standard distances for Europe (e.g. for chemicals) or given average distances by train from Chinese 2004 statistics or own assumptions. This dataset has been developed with the goal to serve a preliminary estimation of the Chinese nuclear chain for the Chinese electricity mix. Hence, it cannot be used for comparisons of conversion infrastrucure among countries.;
UUID: 64116582-5009-3632-a6e8-25a78688a2fd</common:generalComment>
